# Contact sharing: one node as a link, in both directions.
#
# The channel link's sibling, and the half that closes a gap the admin verb could not. A radio
# can already be handed a contact for any node in its roster - but a roster record only exists
# for a node that has *transmitted*, and a node that has transmitted is one the radio could have
# kept for itself. The link is the only way to get a key for a node that has never been heard,
# which is what makes a first direct message to it encryptable instead of impossible.
#
# Three things to watch:
#
#   1. The User section, which has grown a heading and two rows under its four fields. They are
#      here rather than on the Nodes tab because this section *is* the record a contact carries:
#      the names above, and the number and key the radio keeps beside them.
#   2. The contact code screen. The same shape as the channel share screen - the code takes
#      every pixel of the body it can get, the caption under it says whose code it is, and the
#      link itself is last, dim and wrapped rather than cut. The caption is worth more here than
#      on the channel screen: a QR code says nothing to an eye, so the name and node number
#      under it are the only check that the picture is this radio's own.
#   3. It is a *shorter* code than the channel one, because a SharedContact is one node rather
#      than eight channels - so its modules are larger and it scans from further away. That is
#      the version difference doing the work, not a change of scale.
#
# The code is black on white on every theme, which is the one colour pair in this client that
# does not follow the palette; the channel-sharing scene films that rule and it is the same rule
# here, so this scene spends its frames on the screen instead.
#
# The other direction - a link typed in - is the keyboard and then the ordinary confirm sheet,
# both filmed elsewhere. What is new there is the check in front of the sheet, and a refusal is
# not a thing a capture can show usefully.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

tab settings
hold 500

# Into the User section: the four fields that are this radio's owner record, and then the two
# contact rows under their heading.
key down 1
key a
hold 1400
key down 4
hold 1800

# The code. This radio's name, number and public key as one square a phone adds in a press.
key a
hold 2800

key b
hold 800
